From: OpenWrt USG-PRO-4 maintainers <openwrt-devel@lists.openwrt.org>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: octeon: associate bootbus MTD with its OF node

The Octeon bootbus flash driver predates OF-aware MTD partition and
NVMEM handling.  Associate the map and resulting MTD device with the
platform device's OF node so command-line partitions can be matched to
their fixed-partition nodes and expose nested NVMEM layouts.

---
 arch/mips/cavium-octeon/flash_setup.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/mips/cavium-octeon/flash_setup.c
+++ b/arch/mips/cavium-octeon/flash_setup.c
@@ -99,6 +99,7 @@ static int octeon_flash_probe(struct pla
 		flash_map.size = 0x1fc00000 - flash_map.phys;
 		/* 8-bit bus (0 + 1) or 16-bit bus (1 + 1) */
 		flash_map.bankwidth = region_cfg.s.width + 1;
+		flash_map.device_node = np;
 		flash_map.virt = ioremap(flash_map.phys, flash_map.size);
 		pr_notice("Bootbus flash: Setting flash for %luMB flash at "
 			  "0x%08llx\n", flash_map.size >> 20, flash_map.phys);
@@ -110,6 +111,8 @@ static int octeon_flash_probe(struct pla
 		mymtd = do_map_probe("cfi_probe", &flash_map);
 		if (mymtd) {
 			mymtd->owner = THIS_MODULE;
+			mymtd->dev.parent = &pdev->dev;
+			mtd_set_of_node(mymtd, np);
 			mtd_device_parse_register(mymtd, part_probe_types,
 						  NULL, NULL, 0);
 		} else {
